WEBVTT

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.630
Ako!

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.260
Good morning!

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.400
Morning, when's the bus coming?

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.520
In three minutes!

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:45.980
Shizu.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.610
Heya, transfer student!

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.010
You're quite frilly again today.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.010
Is that what's in style in Tokyo?

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.620
This is my own preference.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.240
And a very minor one.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.710
You're living it, huh?

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.460
By the way, could you stop calling me

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.750
"transfer student" or "frilly" already?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.880
Oh, what should we call you then?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.230
My name is Nodoka.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.010
Haramura Nodoka.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.350
I like it. Then...

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.480
Let's be friends.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.480
Yeah.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.780
Let's be friends,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.830
Nodoka!

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:45.350
<b>Episode 1
Chance meeting</b>

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.250
You're slow, Nodoka!

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.630
I bet you don't get regular exercise!

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:56.700
I-It's just that you guys are too fast...

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.300
And why did you 
suddenly start sprinting?

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.450
Are you children or what?

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.180
We are!

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.280
So this is what they mean 
by "frail city kid."

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.230
Nodoka, hurry up!

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.650
Nodoka!

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:15.890
Are you okay?

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.930
That looked painful.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.860
I'm... fine...

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:24.120
Is there something you're good at?

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.630
Other than studying?

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.700
You're already excluding studying?

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.790
Let's see...

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.460
If I had to pick something, 
I guess it would be mahjong.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.720
Mahjong?!

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.980
What, seriously?

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.390
This is...

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.810
<b>Achiga Girls' Academy</b>

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.810
Achiga...

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.900
A girls' school in a place like this?

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.230
A place like this meaning 
"out in the boonies"?

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.740
You're looking down on us!

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.670
You might not think so,

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.000
but this is a fancy middle and 
high school for young ladies.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.800
Very few students, but still.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.980
I see.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.080
Nodoka, let's go.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.460
We can go in?!

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.060
They already know us around here.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.370
Nodoka!

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.420
Over here!

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.900
Achiga Children's Mahjong Club
 Beginners welcome!

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.900
A mahjong class?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.870
So this is this club's room?

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.150
Yeah, but the club 
doesn't exist any more.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.360
Excuse us.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.110
That's it!

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:44.890
Riichi.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.560
There are so many children here...

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:48.820
Heya.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.410
It's Ako-chan!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.240
Ako-chan!

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.630
Nodoka, I'll introduce you.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.620
Keep making a pair in mind more.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.640
Okay.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.530
Sensei!

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.680
Shizu. It's been quite a while.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.080
Around this time, I have to 
help out at home quite a bit.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.270
I see. Who's this?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.390
A promising newcomer.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.780
Indeed, your future 
looks quite interesting.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.810
What were you looking 
at when you said that?!

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.480
My name's Akado Harue.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.740
I'm a college student who's teaching

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.460
the kids here mahjong.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:28.370
And who are you?

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.260
My name's Haramura Nodoka. 
I'm a sixth year in elementary school.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.540
All right,

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.470
shall we give it a shot then?

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.540
Come on!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.910
Tsumo. 2000-4000.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:14.290
(Points to be paid by the non-dealers and the dealer. 
Tsumo - Declaring a winning hand on your draw.)

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.290
Wow!

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.650
Oh man, Nodoka won.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.980
Oh, you're not bad.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.090
I don't know. I think one East-South match

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.090
is not enough to determine one's skill.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:27.850
I guess so. Then let's call her.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.400
Roger!

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.140
She's coming!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.770
Who are you calling?

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:41.510
Nodoka, don't get full of yourself 
just because you beat us.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:46.360
In this club, me and Shizu 
are number 2 and 3,

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.860
but the one who's coming now

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.330
is the number 1!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.500
Matsumi Kuro, reporting for duty!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.840
Kuro-chan!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.520
Oh, we have someone new.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.030
Nice to meet you!

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.480
Nice to meet you...

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.090
Oh my,

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.800
you're so young, but you already have

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:15.810
as much or more than my sister...

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.440
Stop the sexual harassment.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.060
<i>Like you're innocent...</i>

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.600
I am terribly sorry.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.770
Heya.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.200
My name's Matsumi Kuro.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.360
I'm a first year in this academy's 
middle school section.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.200
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.000
Likewise.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.530
2nd Match, South 4, 
Dealer - Matsumi Kuro

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:40.070
So you're the booby transfer 
student Ako-chan talked about.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.350
Don't tell her!

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.140
But you really said so.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:47.250
Still, that's not cool!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.440
Um, were the red dora taken out?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:56.260
(Note: The red dora are four optional tiles with red 
images which count as dora in a winning hand.)

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.010
And I haven't seen a standard dora until now,

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.020
and it's the last hand.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.790
If you say that,

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.530
you're giving away that 
you don't have any.

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:08.520
Though I guess there's no 
way that you'd get any.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.320
Huh? What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.700
The reason we haven't 
seen any dora is because

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.580
Kuro hasn't revealed her hand once.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:19.200
All dora go to Kuro!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.170
That kind of superstition doesn't happen!

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.210
Whoa.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.500
That's it. 8000!

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.710
And that's it.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.870
Kuro, show us your hand.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:31.760
Yes.

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.380
This is the first time I've seen a 
red tile in this East-South match,

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:40.650
and you have all four...

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.230
What's more, you have eight dora!

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.670
Mysterious, eh?

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.980
No, this must be a coincidence!

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.740
Why don't we play another round

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.870
to find out if it's a coincidence or not.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.410
Why are you getting all cocky?

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.660
All right.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.960
Then let's go to the next match.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.310
Okay!

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:08.600
Man, I haven't played until I 
got tired in a long time.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:12.040
In the end, all the dora 
went to Kuro, didn't they?

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.470
That was just coincidence.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.340
If it happens 10 times in a row,

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.970
I'll think of another reason.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.970
I'm glad that you play mahjong.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.410
There aren't very many kids around here

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.480
and when it comes to mahjong 
players, there're even less.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.550
Basically the only people 
over elementary year four

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:30.480
that go there are Ako, Kuro-san, and me.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.430
It would be great if you 
decide to go there regularly,

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.450
because then we'd have more opportunities

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:37.260
to play matches with just us older kids.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.370
So, how about it?!

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.920
If I'm not imposing...

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:46.740
Yay!

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:51.590
All right. Now we have...

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.840
something new to look forward to!

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.120
Happy Birthday, Akado-sensei

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:34.920
Yup!

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.850
Hanging out with you guys is fun!

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:51.010
Oh, I was wondering.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:55.280
If Akado-san is in college, 
why is she taking

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.860
the time to run a mahjong class here?

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:01.830
I guess you don't know about Akado 
Harue since you transferred here.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:05.920
There's a really strong high school called

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.340
Bansei High School 
here in Nara prefecture.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.250
Their mahjong club has 
existed for about 40 years

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.090
and have breezed through the 
prefectural tournaments

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.190
basically every year to move 
on to the national tournament.

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:16.860
Bansei High has lost

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.640
the prefectural tournament just once.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.390
That was six years ago,

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:24.390
and they were beaten by our own 
Achiga Girls' Mahjong Club.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:28.380
The star at the time was the 
then high school first year

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.850
Akado Harue - Achiga's legend!

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:33.810
Lege... but if she's that good,

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.810
couldn't she play in 
intercollegiate championships

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:40.820
or go professional, instead 
of dealing with us kids?

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.160
You're right, but actually,

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.910
Achiga's team six years ago was on a

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.620
furious streak until the semi finals.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:53.420
However, during the semi finals,

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.920
Akado-san lost a huge number 
of points and lost.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:58.790
After that,

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:02.140
she couldn't even touch 
any tiles for a while.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.790
That's why the star of the club quit,

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.550
and the other good players, 
who were third years, graduated.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:13.820
The next year, Achiga 
lost in the first match.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:17.470
That's why the mahjong club was disbanded

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.190
and why this is the status quo.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:22.460
I suppose anybody who really 
wants to play mahjong around here

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:24.350
goes to Bansei High anyway.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:27.680
The fact that we had strong 
players at Achiga six years ago

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:29.160
was kind of a miracle.

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:34.130
I heard that Akado-san is doing 
this class as a sort of rehab.

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:35.630
Rehab?

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:39.210
I think her teammate, 
Ako's sister, recommended it.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.080
Yup, yup.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.650
But if she was that good before,

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.150
won't she quit doing this

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.810
once she's done with her rehab?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:52.730
No...

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.980
That can't happen!

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:59.930
But... wouldn't it be a 
good thing for Akado-san

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:01.780
to get back to actively playing?

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:04.830
Yeah...

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.390
This place...

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.560
will go away?

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.420
Mom, the bath is free.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:31.810
Okay. Hey...

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.520
What?

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.540
They're showing a mahjong 
title match on TV.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.840
Don't you want to watch it?

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:37.760
No...

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.270
Oh, I see.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:43.530
This is the one who made 
Achiga Girls' lose six years ago.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.070
Kokaji declares <i>riichi</i>!

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.070
(Riichi - Declaring you are one tile away from winning and putting 
1000 points into the pot for a chance to further increase your score)

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.990
Kokaji Sukoya, the youngest 
player with eight titles in history!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:53.040
This riichi is a step toward 
a historical first 9th title!

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:56.440
See ya.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.660
Yeah, I'll send you a text later.

00:13:03.270 --> 00:13:05.680
I like the uniform of this school.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.180
Why don't you borrow it from Kuro-san?

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.080
No, I meant that I'd like 
to wear it properly.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.430
So you'll be coming here next year?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.760
Yes, I think I'd like to.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:16.470
I think I'll do the same.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.020
I like the club here.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.570
I think I might go to Ada Middle School.

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:26.280
I want to play mahjong.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:29.160
Achiga doesn't have a club anymore.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:33.980
For mahjong, Ada Middle School 
is the strongest around here.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:37.500
Then, I guess you'll move 
up to Bansei for high school.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.830
I see.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.320
But let's play from time to time.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:42.500
Of course!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:47.220
Excuse us.

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:50.050
Yes, indeed.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.310
I remembered the tournament 
from that year

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.180
and checked all your matches.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:55.180
Who's she talking to?

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:59.840
Apparently she's the coach of 
a corporate team from Fukuoka.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:01.770
That's amazing.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.160
Corporate team?

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.030
She's being scouted?!

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:11.190
That's great, Harue!

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.350
So that was a scout 
from a corporate team?

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:16.240
Yeah, apparently she looked 
at my old match records.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.580
That's great!

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.580
Achiga's legend is finally being revived!

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.090
Akado Harue's Farewell Party

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:30.590
Akado-sensei, congratulations!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:33.350
Thank you for all you've done for us!

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.350
No, I want to thank you.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.140
While teaching you guys mahjong here

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.860
and seeing how you enjoyed yourselves,

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.900
I remembered how much I used 
to love mahjong myself.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:48.240
So... this is all thanks to you guys.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:51.740
So, thank you, everyone!

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:30.490
Nodoka!

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:31.930
Shizuno!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.310
I guess in the end,

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:41.430
we don't even hang out with 
Ako after school any more.

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:43.080
You're right.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:46.470
We haven't seen Akado-san 
even once since then, either.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:50.140
Are we all just going to 
drift apart like this?

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:57.100
I think I probably won't 
be here next spring, either.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.810
What?! Why?!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:03.030
My mother's work transfers 
her every two to three years.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.560
The next time will probably 
be next spring...

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.490
I'm sorry.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.820
Don't worry about it.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:16.380
I had kind of prepared 
myself ever since I knew

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.880
that we wouldn't be in the same class.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:20.290
I guess that's the way the world is.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.420
I mean, I've made friends 
in my new class, too.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:28.000
Well, get in touch if something happens.

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.330
Takakamo Shizuno

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.330
Achiga Girls' Middle School
Third year

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.520
Heya.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.840
As energetic as usual.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.840
I'm home!

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:18.240
<i>Today's topic is this! Nara's...</i>

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:22.120
It really is summer break; 
there's nothing good on TV.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.980
<i>These are the finals of the</i>

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.060
<i>National Middle School
 Mahjong Individual Tournament!</i>

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.060
Oh, what have we here?

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:29.100
I did play a bit of that in my youth.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.020
<i>Currently in the lead is 
Haramura Nodoka from</i>

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:30.540
Let's see how they do.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.730
<i>Nagano prefecture's 
Takatoubara Middle School.</i>

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:42.810
<i>Haramura Nodoka is making a 
move, she's declared riichi!</i>

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.260
<i>Tsumo!</i>

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:50.480
<i>Haramura Nodoka has finished 
the last hand with a tsumo!</i>

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:51.820
<i>The winner of the individual tournament is</i>

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:55.100
<i>Takatoubara Middle School 
third year, Haramura Nodoka!</i>

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.970
Why am I running?!

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.060
What should I do?!

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:05.430
Should I call her to congratulate her?

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.550
But something like pride 
is not allowing me to.

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:11.360
Not that I have her number or anything...

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.860
Hello? Ako?

00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:19.990
Oh, Shizu? It's been ages.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.820
What's up all of a sudden?

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.910
TV? Yeah, I watched it. 
You mean Nodoka, right?

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.230
I was really surprised, too.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.710
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.570
You're the best person I know

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:34.170
to talk to about this weird feeling, too.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.760
I want to play in that tournament, too!

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.620
You can't do that.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:41.430
Why not?

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:44.290
What do you mean why? 
We're in our last year of middle school.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:46.870
We can't play in the inter-middle 
tournaments anymore.

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:49.350
High school? You want to play in 
the inter-high school tournament?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.400
Then you need to get into Bansei High.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:54.020
The deviation score on their exams is 70.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.010
I'm totally fine, but are 
you going to make it?

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:59.110
Then I'll go to the nationals 
through Achiga Girls'!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.320
Achiga doesn't have a mahjong club

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.870
and if you find club members, 
you won't beat Bansei.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.730
I'm going to Bansei so 
I'll be your opponent.

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:08.750
Fine!

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.000
Ack, I did it again.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.450
Shizu really doesn't 
know how to calculate.

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:21.450
If we could go to the 
nationals with Achiga,

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.510
I would have gone there, too.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:47.540
It's open...

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.150
The curtains, too.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.210
The table is here. No dust either...

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.030
Why?

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:05.680
You're finally here.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:09.110
Kuro-san!

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:11.640
I knew you'd come back here eventually.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.190
So you were doing the cleaning here?

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.740
Yes, it's my turn on Thursdays.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:22.330
Turn... you mean the schedule 
we had for mahjong class?

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:22.880
Yes.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.970
You stuck to it for over two years?!

00:20:24.970 --> 00:20:27.890
Well, if I kept up the routine,

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:31.660
I figured that someone 
might come here again,

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:33.800
like back then...

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:36.710
Back then...

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:45.510
Kuro-san, I want to play mahjong here again!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:47.550
With everybody!

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:54.350
I felt the same way this whole time.

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.480
And I want to go to the nationals!

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:01.560
We need to revive the Achiga 
Mahjong Club by spring

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.150
and fight in the 
inter-high school tournament!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.150
Nationals? That's sudden.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:07.500
But it sounds fun!

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:08.720
I know, right?!

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:11.050
I bet Nodoka will be there.

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:12.200
Nodoka-chan?

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:16.100
That way, we can all 
play together again.

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:17.670
If we keep playing mahjong,

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.720
some time, somewhere, we will meet again!

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:23.020
Then first we have to start a club.

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.990
At this school, an interest 
group only needs two people,

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:26.970
so let's start there.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.440
Once we have five people,

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.090
we can convert it to a full club!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:33.870
But finding five people

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:37.150
when we have so few 
students might be a bit...

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:40.610
...tough.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:45.450
You've got your first member here!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.100
Ako-chan!

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:49.950
Ako, I thought you were going to Bansei.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.260
If you and I are in the same school,

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:54.330
we can face Nodoka together.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:57.000
At the nationals!

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:00.830
Let's have a blast together again!

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:03.760
And let's go to the nationals!

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:06.300
Let's go play with Nodoka!

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:10.380
Yeah.

00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:13.400
Let's go play with Nodoka!

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.280
Noddo-chan!

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:53.410
Let's play!

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:03.330
To Shizuno,
How are you

00:23:58.720 --> 00:24:00.250
I'm coming.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:19.890
<b>Beginning</b>

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:09.840
Hey, since it's getting warm, 
how about going bowling?

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:10.790
Sounds good!

00:24:10.790 --> 00:24:15.880
Oh no, the 3, 6 and 9 pins are left.

00:24:15.880 --> 00:24:18.310
Since your wait is so flexible, 
you can get a spare.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:19.220
Huh?

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:25.000
<b>Be sure to watch the next episode, too!</b>
